         /app/requirements.txt|'                                                
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/missing
         _dependency_requirements/Dockerfile                                    
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         2. Rebuild the image (use minikube image build when current kubectl    
         context is minikube; otherwise use local docker). This single script   
         detects minikube and builds appropriately.                             
         ```bash                                                                
         #!/bin/bash                                                            
         DOCKERFILE="/home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshoo
         ting/missing_dependency_requirements/Dockerfile"                       
         CONTEXT_DIR="/home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troublesho
         oting/missing_dependency_requirements"                                 
         IMAGE="kube-missing-dependency-requirements-app:latest"                
                                                                                
         if command -v minikube >/dev/null 2>&1 && kubectl config               
         current-context | grep -qi minikube; then                              
           PROFILE=${MINIKUBE_PROFILE:-$(kubectl config current-context)}       
           minikube -p "$PROFILE" image build -t "$IMAGE" -f "$DOCKERFILE"      
         "$CONTEXT_DIR"                                                         
         else                                                                   
           docker build -t "$IMAGE" -f "$DOCKERFILE" "$CONTEXT_DIR"             
         fi                                                                     
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         3. Redeploy the Pod so Kubernetes picks up the rebuilt local image (the
         manifest uses imagePullPolicy: Never)                                  
         ```bash                                                                
         kubectl delete -f                                                      
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/missing
         _dependency_requirements/missing_dependency_requirements.yaml          
         --ignore-not-found                                                     
         kubectl apply -f                                                       
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/missing
         _dependency_requirements/missing_dependency_requirements.yaml          
         kubectl wait --for=condition=ready                                     
         pod/kube-missing-dependency-requirements --timeout=60s || true         
         kubectl logs pod/kube-missing-dependency-requirements --tail=200       
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         4. Verify the server responds (one-shot check from inside the pod using
         Python's stdlib)                                                       
         ```bash                                                                
         kubectl exec pod/kube-missing-dependency-requirements -- python3 -c    
         "import urllib.request,sys;                                            
         print(urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8765').getcode())"      
